1
00:00:01,890 --> 00:00:03,690
Yeah,

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,490
there is someone I like.

3
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:14,960
I…

4
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:19,760
love Reo Amano.

5
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,680
Then that makes us rivals.

6
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,650
This feels so nostalgic.

7
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:37,730
Many girls used to declare war to me over Reo.

8
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:43,230
I didn't lose back in middle school,

9
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:46,480
however...

10
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:50,540
Mai, was it?

11
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:52,620
His current girlfriend?

12
00:00:55,890 --> 00:00:58,690
It seems romance never goes well.

13
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:12,210
<i>[Ai-Chan's Secret | Episode 9]</i>

14
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:25,760
Things aren't over within Yuka's heart.

15
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:32,130
She's always wholeheartedly loved Reo.

16
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:37,860
When I saw Yuka like that,

17
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:42,530
I felt like I needed to be honest, even if it spilled my secret.

18
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:51,030
So you told her you love Reo, and now it's like you two are comrades.

19
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:54,880
Yeah, something like that.

20
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:57,620
And now you're feeling unsure?

21
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:05,010
Were you also frustrated that you couldn't say, “I’m Mai”?

22
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:10,470
Yeah. I thought I was being unfair.

23
00:02:13,950 --> 00:02:16,910
Jeez, you're so honest when you're in love!

24
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:21,970
You don't need to be considerate of his ex.

25
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:24,880
You're Reo's current girlfriend.

26
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:31,260
But I don't think Reo broke up because he wanted to either.

27
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:34,120
An ex-girlfriend

28
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:39,810
knows a version of our partner, unknown to us.

29
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:46,350
We become uneasy, because that's unchangeable.

30
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:48,700
Yeah.

31
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:52,190
Even so, Reo says it's over.

32
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:54,330
All we can do is believe him.

33
00:02:57,870 --> 00:03:01,470
That's what I've decided to do.

34
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:09,210
Which means… you've forgiven Ritsuki?

35
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:10,890
Yes.

36
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,490
I'm a fool, aren't I?

37
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:20,860
Despite it all, I love him.

38
00:03:22,690 --> 00:03:24,820
That's why

39
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,330
I'll believe in Ritsuki.

40
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,830
I see.

41
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:44,780
<i>[Just finished my shift. What are you up to?]</i>

42
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:51,050
<i>He's probably</i>

43
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:54,300
<i>at his part-time job... right?</i>

44
00:03:56,650 --> 00:03:59,110
<i>You're the one who let go,</i>

45
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,980
<i>Yuka.</i>

46
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:08,310
<i>[Kafuu High School]</i>

47
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:12,260
Wow, seriously?

48
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:14,250
Is Reo's ex that much of a beauty?

49
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:18,520
Yeah, she won the pageant at her middle school, and her personality's great.

50
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:20,150
<i>That's amazing!</i>

51
00:04:20,150 --> 00:04:22,770
Then, Reo confessed to her.

52
00:04:22,770 --> 00:04:24,910
- For real?!
- For real.

53
00:04:24,910 --> 00:04:26,890
Of course they suit one another.

54
00:04:26,890 --> 00:04:30,730
It was a real spectacle.

55
00:04:30,730 --> 00:04:32,840
Tell me the details.

56
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:34,630
Sure.

57
00:04:34,630 --> 00:04:37,230
Why not chase them and ask?

58
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:40,190
I don't want to know.

59
00:04:40,190 --> 00:04:44,990
That ex was the exact opposite of you.

60
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,010
Are you jealous?

61
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:50,030
I'm not.

62
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:55,920
His ex-girlfriend may be more stubborn than anticipated.

63
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:00,910
Takumi,

64
00:05:00,910 --> 00:05:05,820
are you one to quickly forget about a girl you liked?

65
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:09,400
You're gonna ask me?

66
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,290
Sorry.

67
00:05:16,130 --> 00:05:20,430
Let yourself be vulnerable, and I'll kiss you.

68
00:05:20,430 --> 00:05:23,400
You idiot. What the hell.

69
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,230
Are you worried about Reo?

70
00:05:27,230 --> 00:05:29,120
Not really.

71
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,900
Don't worry. You have

72
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:35,310
your own, unique charms.

73
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:38,720
That's none of your business.

74
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,650
Thanks.

75
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,340
- I want to buy new sneakers.
- Same here.

76
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:06,150
- Really?
- Yeah, my current ones don't support my ankles.

77
00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:08,040
- Makes sense.
- What're you guys talking about?

78
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:10,640
- Buying new basketball shoes.
- For Reo?

79
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:15,080
<i>[Do you have time after practice today?]</i>

80
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,970
<i>[Sorry, I have plans today]</i>

81
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:29,120
<i>[I'll make time for you]</i>

82
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:35,470
Did Reo leave?

83
00:06:35,470 --> 00:06:38,530
Yes, he seemed to be in a hurry.

84
00:06:38,530 --> 00:06:40,570
- Yeah.
- Maybe he has a date?

85
00:06:40,570 --> 00:06:43,260
Possibly.

86
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:46,520
Thanks.

87
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,390
Thank you!

88
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:56,130
Thank you for your patronage!

89
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:04,950
Why?

90
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:08,280
Ken told me.

91
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,820
That bastard.

92
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:16,910
How long have you been with Reo?

93
00:07:16,910 --> 00:07:18,800
How long...?

94
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:21,010
How long have you two been dating?

95
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:25,640
About three months.

96
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:28,660
Thank goodness.

97
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:33,100
See you again.

98
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,580
Well...

99
00:07:38,490 --> 00:07:41,680
Don't you have business with Reo?

100
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:46,360
I'll try another day. It's something I can't discuss around you.

101
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,450
Give up on him.

102
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:57,430
It's not that easy.

103
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:08,700
Good work.

104
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:12,900
Aiko?

105
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:23,200
Sorry. To tell you the truth,

106
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:26,940
Hiroko, Ikumi and I tailed you the other day.

107
00:08:27,730 --> 00:08:29,550
For real?

108
00:08:30,230 --> 00:08:32,950
I'm sure you're put off by that.

109
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,410
Not at all.

110
00:08:38,230 --> 00:08:39,960
I'm happy.

111
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:49,000
You could've told me about your part-time job.

112
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:53,340
Isn't there something else you want to say?

113
00:09:04,810 --> 00:09:06,700
I'll listen to every last thing

114
00:09:08,210 --> 00:09:10,500
you want to tell me.

115
00:09:11,990 --> 00:09:14,680
That's why you came, right?

116
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:27,380
You won't hate me?

117
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:29,310
Of course I won't.

118
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:34,820
I don't know what to do.

119
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:37,510
I wonder what you're doing after practice.

120
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:41,220
I feel down, just because you haven't read my texts.

121
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,800
I anxiously think about how you may be seeing Yuka.

122
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:46,920
I don't want to think about it, and I want to believe you.

123
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:52,400
But I keep thinking about how you might choose Yuka after all.

124
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:57,200
It's the first time I've loved someone this much.

125
00:09:58,410 --> 00:10:00,400
Reo,

126
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:05,800
you're the first person I've ever dated.

127
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:08,180
I don't know what to do.

128
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,240
And today, I—

129
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:17,560
Wow,

130
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:20,280
I totally lost my cool.

131
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:24,570
That wasn't what I wanted to say.

132
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:28,280
I'm really

133
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:30,010
sorry.

134
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:33,180
Aiko...

135
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:49,320
<i>[I'll be returning to Kagoshima the day after tomorrow]</i>

136
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:52,710
<i>[Can we meet, one last time?]</i>

137
00:10:58,590 --> 00:11:01,010
That was so uncool.

138
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:02,990
So unlike me.

139
00:11:02,990 --> 00:11:05,860
Let's eat and forget all about it.

140
00:11:07,070 --> 00:11:10,100
- What does it mean to be "like oneself"?
- Huh?

141
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:13,520
So, what does it mean to be, "Aiko"?

142
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:17,240
"More manly then men",

143
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:20,280
and, "the ace of our girls basketball team"?

144
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:24,860
It's unlike me to overthink things.

145
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:31,280
Yet, I ambushed him with so much.

146
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:33,830
Now it's awkward, and I'm embarrassed.

147
00:11:33,830 --> 00:11:36,450
What's wrong with being uncool?

148
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:41,970
Romance isn't all about showing your good side.

149
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:49,500
You discovered new sides to yourself, and told him how you felt, despite the mess.

150
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:52,130
You're not uncool at all.

151
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,360
Reo...

152
00:12:35,510 --> 00:12:39,230
Sorry I made you anxious.

153
00:12:48,650 --> 00:12:51,110
I'm going to end it, for good.

154
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:58,130
Will you come with me tonight?

155
00:13:16,350 --> 00:13:18,290
A confrontation with his ex-girlfriend?

156
00:13:18,290 --> 00:13:19,480
Seems like it.

157
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,450
Where? I'll go too.

158
00:13:21,450 --> 00:13:22,890
Ikumi.

159
00:13:22,890 --> 00:13:25,700
I'm worried if it's just Mai.

160
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:29,140
That other girl is aggressively aiming for Reo.

161
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:31,340
Look at a mirror before saying that.

162
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:33,390
Mai is too kind for her own good.

163
00:13:33,390 --> 00:13:36,820
That's what makes her charming.

164
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:40,030
I thought you were loyal to Ai?

165
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:43,500
The order is up.

166
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:46,670
- Okay.
- Okay.

167
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,720
Actually, I'll—

168
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,520
Stay seated.

169
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:16,770
Thank you for waiting. Here is your coffee.

170
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:23,550
Please enjoy.

171
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,850
Yuka...

172
00:14:31,850 --> 00:14:36,470
I have no intention of meeting behind her back.

173
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,000
If you're okay with that,

174
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,250
I'll listen to whatever you have to say.

175
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,650
That's all right.

176
00:14:48,830 --> 00:14:51,470
After all, I don't want to hold any more regrets.

177
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:56,930
I wanted to explain what happened back then.

178
00:15:08,390 --> 00:15:11,560
My stomach… I'm going to the restroom!

179
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:21,530
Her intentions are plain as day.

180
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:23,880
You can't hate her, can you?

181
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:30,550
I see.

182
00:15:30,550 --> 00:15:33,730
I'm no longer a part of you.

183
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,540
Even so...

184
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:46,770
you still remain within me.

185
00:15:50,970 --> 00:15:54,480
To be honest,

186
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,680
I know why you left without a word.

187
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:00,600
I heard your parents divorced,

188
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,270
and you went with your mother.

189
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:06,690
There was the option to have a long distance relationship,

190
00:16:06,690 --> 00:16:10,550
but you had us break up, cause I was weak, right?

191
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,780
- No.
- "Long distance is impossible,

192
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:14,700
and it'd be unbearable..."

193
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:17,120
That's what I would've said back then.

194
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,400
No, that's not it.

195
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:23,150
I thought distance would cause misunderstandings.

196
00:16:23,150 --> 00:16:26,370
If we were to hurt one another and break up, then I'd rather...

197
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:30,500
I didn't want to hate you, Reo.

198
00:16:36,490 --> 00:16:38,770
Even so,

199
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:42,520
I seriously loved you.

200
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:46,830
I wanted to face those issues, and find answers, together.

201
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:57,460
You're right.

202
00:16:58,330 --> 00:17:01,120
Now, I agree with you.

203
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:13,160
Yuka, you'll never disappear

204
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:16,130
from within me.

205
00:17:20,550 --> 00:17:23,660
You're the first person I seriously loved.

206
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:28,130
However, neither time

207
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,820
nor feelings

208
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,860
can return to what they use to be.

209
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:43,300
She made me realize something.

210
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,920
<i>You're really good! </i>

211
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:51,180
<i>Say… Let’s join the basketball club together!</i>

212
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:56,130
<i>I'm Aiko Kasumi.</i>

213
00:17:58,130 --> 00:18:00,010
She made me realize

214
00:18:01,030 --> 00:18:02,910
I'd try falling in love again.

215
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:05,730
♫ <i>What awaits in this battle of love?</i> ♫

216
00:18:05,730 --> 00:18:08,600
♫ <i>It seems it won't end in a draw</i> ♫

217
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:10,230
♫ <i>You hated loosing,</i> ♫

218
00:18:10,230 --> 00:18:11,640
How shameful of me.

219
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,880
♫ <i>So I won't let you go easy on me</i> ♫

220
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:18,390
Reo, you've moved on a long time ago.

221
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:28,910
♫ <i>I don't wish for anyone to know my secret</i> ♫

222
00:18:28,910 --> 00:18:31,950
♫ <i>I want to steal you away</i> ♫

223
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:34,010
♫ <i>The secret that belongs to only us.</i> ♫

224
00:18:34,010 --> 00:18:35,830
Yuka!

225
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:40,140
I'm sorry.

226
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:43,610
I need to be honest with you.

227
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:48,400
I'm... actually—

228
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,340
Wait.

229
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:52,270
Aiko?

230
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,510
As I thought.

231
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:01,470
So, you realized.

232
00:19:01,470 --> 00:19:05,030
On our second… no, third meeting?

233
00:19:05,030 --> 00:19:07,610
When we saw each other at Reo's part-time job,

234
00:19:07,610 --> 00:19:09,940
I thought you two sounded similar.

235
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,880
So you're his girlfriend, Aiko.

236
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:21,860
- I'm sorry.
- Don't apologize.

237
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:26,130
The fact that I’m Reo’s first girlfriend,

238
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:28,830
will now be something you remember.

239
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:33,000
That makes us even.

240
00:19:34,850 --> 00:19:41,150
♫ <i>Rather than touching, we can melt
into one another's embrace</i> ♫

241
00:19:41,150 --> 00:19:46,950
♫ <i>I'll let you get near just to return you like a wave</i> ♫

242
00:19:46,950 --> 00:19:49,060
This is the end.

243
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,990
♫ <i>Lips to exchange</i> ♫

244
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:57,110
Good bye.

245
00:20:07,750 --> 00:20:11,380
Meddlesome, reckless, selfish.

246
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:13,990
How else should I describe you?

247
00:20:13,990 --> 00:20:15,850
Reo...

248
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:19,140
are you mad?

249
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:20,660
No.

250
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:25,990
Let's go home.

251
00:20:31,610 --> 00:20:35,570
You're not curious to hear what we talked about?

252
00:20:42,690 --> 00:20:45,560
The memories you two share...

253
00:20:46,990 --> 00:20:49,550
should stay between you two.

254
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:53,370
That's why

255
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,410
I don't need to know.

256
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:10,590
When I spoke with Yuka,

257
00:21:11,290 --> 00:21:13,850
there was something I remembered.

258
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,650
I want

259
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:24,430
to break up with "Mai".

260
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:30,780
Instead,

261
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:34,180
I want to date "Aiko".

262
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:40,920
I didn't fall for you as "Mai".

263
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:42,920
The one I love,

264
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:45,180
is none other then "Aiko Kasumi".

265
00:21:55,030 --> 00:21:57,300
<i>[Kasumi]</i>

266
00:22:02,540 --> 00:22:04,560
<i>Next Sunday, </i>

267
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:07,790
<i>I want you to come as Aiko. For real this time.</i>

268
00:22:10,410 --> 00:22:12,510
Game face, on.

269
00:22:12,510 --> 00:22:16,270
- I'm sleepy.
- Today's herbal tea will be chamomile.

270
00:22:16,270 --> 00:22:17,440
